course: dictionary
lesson: 12398
title: Words about rules and time
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A curfew is a rule about time. It says that people must be indoors, or at home, by a certain hour, usually at night. «Maya's curfew is nine o'clock, so she has to be home before then.» The time is the clue: a curfew is a deadline.
explain: Look at the words around curfew to work out its meaning. Words such as home, indoors and by nine tell you it is about being inside at a set time. A curfew can be set by parents for their children, or by a government during an emergency.
explain: In history, a curfew was a bell. «In the Middle Ages, the curfew rang in the evening, and people put out their fires.» It is a different use of the word, but the idea is the same: a signal that a set time has come.
fact: A curfew is a rule that says people must be indoors or at home by a certain time.
fact: «Curfew» most often means the time a child or teenager must be home, set by their parents.
fact: «Impose a curfew» means to set a curfew, often a government rule during a war, riots or an emergency.
fact: «Break a curfew» means to be out after the time you were told to be home.
fact: In the Middle Ages, the curfew was a bell rung in the evening, telling people to put out their fires.
exercise: «Maya's curfew is nine o'clock.» What is a curfew? | A party held in the evening | A kind of shoe | *A time by which you must be indoors or at home | A special bell rung at lunchtime
exercise: «The leaders imposed a curfew after the riots.» What does a curfew mean here? | A prize for the best team | A new type of bus | *A rule to stay indoors from a certain time | A long walk in the park
exercise: «Tom broke his curfew by coming home at midnight.» What does broke a curfew mean? | Lost his way to school | *Was out after the time he was told to be home | Ate his dinner too fast | Broke a window at home
test: «After curfew, the streets were empty.» What does after curfew mean? | During a football match | *After the time when people must be indoors | Before breakfast | At the start of the school day
test: Dad says, «Your curfew is half past eight.» What is he telling you? | A new homework task | *A time you must be home by | A type of game | The time the shops open
exam: Which is the best meaning of curfew? | A large meal eaten at lunchtime | *A rule that says people must be indoors by a certain time | A kind of bird that sings at night | A sort of cloud that brings rain
